      "started_at": "2026-11-06T15:08:09.801435+00:00",
      "result": {
        "reply_text": "The Uttar Pradesh Urban Buildings (Regulation of Letting, Rent and Eviction) Act, 1972 is repealed except for certain pending proceedings, and new cases are governed by the Uttar Pradesh Regulation of Urban Premises Tenancy Act, 2021. You can approach the Rent Authority appointed by the District Collector to file an application with an affidavit and documents.\n\nThe security deposit shall be refunded to the tenant on the date of taking over vacant possession of the premises from the tenant, after making due deduction of any liability of the tenant.\n\nKeep your tenancy agreement, proof of payment of the security deposit, and any written communications with the landlord ready.\n\nSource: Uttar Pradesh Regulation of Urban Premises Tenancy Act, 2021, section 46\nSource: Uttar Pradesh Regulation of Urban Premises Tenancy Act, 2021, section 30\nSource: Uttar Pradesh Regulation of Urban Premises Tenancy Act, 2021, section 33\nSource: Uttar Pradesh Regulation of Urban Premises Tenancy Act, 2021, section 11\n\nNote: Uttar Pradesh Urban Buildings (Regulation of Letting, Rent and Eviction) Act, 1972 is no longer in force, so I do not use it.\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
